    ('568520d6-465e-4a57-b7a6-dd5055cf43c6', 0, $$School is over. Children are leaving. Teachers are leaving. Everyone is going home.$$),
    ('568520d6-465e-4a57-b7a6-dd5055cf43c6', 1, $$I come out of the gate. I am in a hurry. I do not have time to play. I do not have time to talk. I want to get home fast.$$),
    ('568520d6-465e-4a57-b7a6-dd5055cf43c6', 2, $$I walk down the lane. It is a narrow lane. I can see crowds up ahead. There is a big road there.$$),
    ('568520d6-465e-4a57-b7a6-dd5055cf43c6', 3, $$The big road has lots of traffic. Cars, trucks and cycles, motorcycles, scooters and auto rickshaws. Some are going this way. Some are going that way. I know how to find the gap and run to the other side.$$),
    ('568520d6-465e-4a57-b7a6-dd5055cf43c6', 4, $$I have reached the divider. There is traffic in front. There is traffic behind. I must be careful.$$),
    ('568520d6-465e-4a57-b7a6-dd5055cf43c6', 5, $$I am on the other side. I almost crash into the chanawallah. He growls. I say, “Sorry,” and run along.$$),
    ('568520d6-465e-4a57-b7a6-dd5055cf43c6', 6, $$I walk faster and faster. Now there are fish shops. Big fish, small fish, long fish, flat fish. Shiny fish, dull fish. So many fish in every shop.$$),
    ('568520d6-465e-4a57-b7a6-dd5055cf43c6', 7, $$I walk faster and faster. Now there are fish shops. Big fish, small fish, long fish, flat fish. Shiny fish, dull fish, So many fish in every shop.$$),
    ('568520d6-465e-4a57-b7a6-dd5055cf43c6', 8, $$Now I must run. Past the video shops, past the barber shop, past the cloth shop, past the pan shop. Running, running, running down the lane.$$),
    ('568520d6-465e-4a57-b7a6-dd5055cf43c6', 9, $$Finally I reach home. Oh good! I am not late. My father goes to work in the afternoon. He has not left as yet. His cycle is still here.$$),
    ('568520d6-465e-4a57-b7a6-dd5055cf43c6', 10, $$My father comes outside, my mother is behind him. I give my father a big hug. My father gives me a big hug. Then he goes to work. Now there is no hurry. I have lots of time.$$),
    ('56b99e82-1b18-4221-b3b1-a045ecc1093c', 0, $$A fawn was racing in the forest.$$),
    ('56b99e82-1b18-4221-b3b1-a045ecc1093c', 1, $$He was ahead of the rabbit.$$),
    ('56b99e82-1b18-4221-b3b1-a045ecc1093c', 2, $$He was ahead of the elephant.$$),
    ('56b99e82-1b18-4221-b3b1-a045ecc1093c', 3, $$He leapt and cleared the stream.$$),
    ('56b99e82-1b18-4221-b3b1-a045ecc1093c', 4, $$He ran past the crumbling wall.$$),
    ('56b99e82-1b18-4221-b3b1-a045ecc1093c', 5, $$There was a large boulder on the grassy plain. He stumbled and fell down.$$),
    ('56b99e82-1b18-4221-b3b1-a045ecc1093c', 6, $$He burst into tears.$$),
    ('56b99e82-1b18-4221-b3b1-a045ecc1093c', 7, $$The monkey massaged his leg. Tears flowed from the fawn's eyes.$$),
    ('56b99e82-1b18-4221-b3b1-a045ecc1093c', 8, $$Brother Bear picked him up. The fawn didn't stop crying.$$),
    ('56b99e82-1b18-4221-b3b1-a045ecc1093c', 9, $$His mother came. She said, “Look, we’ll beat up this bad boulder! ”$$),
    ('56b99e82-1b18-4221-b3b1-a045ecc1093c', 10, $$The fawn said, “Oh, don’t do that or he will also start crying. ” His mother laughed. So did the fawn.$$),
    ('593c881e-afca-42be-8345-c2d8578c912c', 0, $$"Ssss. Ssss. " Someone was whispering in my ear!$$),
    ('593c881e-afca-42be-8345-c2d8578c912c', 1, $$I asked, “Who is there? ”$$),
    ('593c881e-afca-42be-8345-c2d8578c912c', 2, $$“It is me,” someone said.$$),
    ('593c881e-afca-42be-8345-c2d8578c912c', 3, $$“Who are you? ” I asked.$$),
    ('593c881e-afca-42be-8345-c2d8578c912c', 4, $$“I told you, it is only me,” the same voice said.$$),
    ('593c881e-afca-42be-8345-c2d8578c912c', 5, $$“I don’t know anyone called, ‘Only Me’,” I replied. I checked that my mosquito net was tucked in around my bed.$$),
    ('593c881e-afca-42be-8345-c2d8578c912c', 6, $$A voice that sounded very high, and very close to my ear said, "What is your name? "$$),
    ('593c881e-afca-42be-8345-c2d8578c912c', 7, $$I said, "No. What is your name? "$$),
    ('593c881e-afca-42be-8345-c2d8578c912c', 8, $$“Mosquito! ” she answered! And then she bit my ear!$$),
    ('593c881e-afca-42be-8345-c2d8578c912c', 9, $$“Ouch! ” I jumped out of bed and began to search. “I will get revenge on you Mosquito! ” I shouted.$$),
    ('593c881e-afca-42be-8345-c2d8578c912c', 10, $$I am going to kill you Mosquito!!!!$$),
    ('599e7c36-e865-4708-aa29-cbb943080df3', 0, $$There was only one bus in Ebei's village. It was big and blue. It was very noisy.$$),
    ('599e7c36-e865-4708-aa29-cbb943080df3', 1, $$"Tomorrow we will go to town," said Ebei's mother. "We will buy your school uniform. "$$),
    ('599e7c36-e865-4708-aa29-cbb943080df3', 2, $$Ebei was very excited. They would travel in the big blue bus. He could not sleep that night.$$),
    ('599e7c36-e865-4708-aa29-cbb943080df3', 3, $$When his mother came to wake him, Ebei was already dressed.$$),
    ('599e7c36-e865-4708-aa29-cbb943080df3', 4, $$Ebei and his mother walked to the bus stop. They waited for the big blue bus. But the bus did not come.$$),
    ('599e7c36-e865-4708-aa29-cbb943080df3', 5, $$Other people arrived at the bus stop. They complained because the bus was late. "Where is the bus? " they asked.$$),
    ('599e7c36-e865-4708-aa29-cbb943080df3', 6, $$Ebei was worried. "We will not be able to go to town," he thought. "I will not be able to get my uniform. "$$),
    ('599e7c36-e865-4708-aa29-cbb943080df3', 7, $$Some people gave up and went home. Ebei cried. He did not want to go. "We will wait a bit longer," said his mother.$$),
    ('599e7c36-e865-4708-aa29-cbb943080df3', 8, $$Suddenly, they heard a noise. They saw dust in the air. The bus was coming!$$),
    ('599e7c36-e865-4708-aa29-cbb943080df3', 9, $$But this bus was not blue. It was not big. It was red and small. The people did not want to get in this bus.$$),
    ('599e7c36-e865-4708-aa29-cbb943080df3', 10, $$"Get in! Get in! " shouted the driver. "We are very late today," he called. Ebei and his mother got in first. Soon everyone else got in the small red bus.$$),
    ('599e7c36-e865-4708-aa29-cbb943080df3', 11, $$Ebei looked out the window. He saw more people at the bus stop.$$),
    ('599e7c36-e865-4708-aa29-cbb943080df3', 12, $$Even more people were running to catch the bus. But they were too late. The red bus was full. It left for town.$$),
    ('599e7c36-e865-4708-aa29-cbb943080df3', 13, $$"Where is the big blue bus? "asked Ebei's mother. "It broke down," replied the driver. "We are fixing it. It will come tomorrow. "$$),
    ('599e7c36-e865-4708-aa29-cbb943080df3', 14, $$Ebei did not care about the colour of the bus. He did not care about the size. This bus was going to town!$$),
    ('59faeb10-7773-4e68-9579-664f37737f23', 0, $$Once there was a dog named Moti. He had a friend named Raju. They were sitting in an umbrella and playing in the river. It started raining.$$),
    ('59faeb10-7773-4e68-9579-664f37737f23', 1, $$They enjoyed the ride together.$$),
    ('59faeb10-7773-4e68-9579-664f37737f23', 2, $$Suddenly, the dog fell in the river.$$),
    ('59faeb10-7773-4e68-9579-664f37737f23', 3, $$Raju went out of the river. He saw a fishing rope on the bank. He threw the rope towards Moti and saved his life.$$),
    ('59faeb10-7773-4e68-9579-664f37737f23', 4, $$After that they caught many fishes and went home happily.$$),
    ('5ac2b794-4da1-4ee7-b18b-dd573d382db9', 0, $$Our community is big.$$),
    ('5ac2b794-4da1-4ee7-b18b-dd573d382db9', 1, $$There are many houses in our community.$$),
    ('5ac2b794-4da1-4ee7-b18b-dd573d382db9', 2, $$It has a big school.$$),
    ('5ac2b794-4da1-4ee7-b18b-dd573d382db9', 3, $$It has an old bridge.$$),
    ('5ac2b794-4da1-4ee7-b18b-dd573d382db9', 4, $$Our park has a fountain.$$),
    ('5ac2b794-4da1-4ee7-b18b-dd573d382db9', 5, $$People in our community talk a lot.$$),
    ('5ac2b794-4da1-4ee7-b18b-dd573d382db9', 6, $$Our grandfathers tell us stories.$$),
    ('5ac2b794-4da1-4ee7-b18b-dd573d382db9', 7, $$The locals are workers.$$),
    ('5ac2b794-4da1-4ee7-b18b-dd573d382db9', 8, $$Our musicians play a lot of tunes.$$),
    ('5ac2b794-4da1-4ee7-b18b-dd573d382db9', 9, $$We kids learn a lot!$$),
    ('5b22e8be-bf5f-4259-a0d4-cae7d6365a3f', 0, $$In my village, there is a businessman called Dembe.$$),
    ('5b22e8be-bf5f-4259-a0d4-cae7d6365a3f', 1, $$Dembe has a big shop in the village.$$),
    ('5b22e8be-bf5f-4259-a0d4-cae7d6365a3f', 2, $$The shop sells flour, sugar, rice, bananas, and many more things.$$),
    ('5b22e8be-bf5f-4259-a0d4-cae7d6365a3f', 3, $$Dembe and his wife have three children. The children help in the shop during the holidays.$$),
    ('5b22e8be-bf5f-4259-a0d4-cae7d6365a3f', 4, $$Each day, Dembe counts the money they earned.$$),
    ('5b22e8be-bf5f-4259-a0d4-cae7d6365a3f', 5, $$Dembe has a business book. In the book he writes the money they earn each day. He also writes the money he to buy things for the shop.$$),
    ('5b22e8be-bf5f-4259-a0d4-cae7d6365a3f', 6, $$Dembe and his wife can afford a nice house and a car.$$),
    ('5b22e8be-bf5f-4259-a0d4-cae7d6365a3f', 7, $$They also have cows, chickens, and rabbits.$$),
    ('5b22e8be-bf5f-4259-a0d4-cae7d6365a3f', 8, $$This family has a good life. Another year, the children will take over the shop. But first they will finish school.$$),
    ('5e6546b9-dea5-4d32-80dd-ce5e29fb0b35', 0, $$It was holiday time. Veena and Vinay were in the garden. There were tins of paint everywhere.$$),
    ('5e6546b9-dea5-4d32-80dd-ce5e29fb0b35', 1, $$There was white paint and red paint and green paint and blue paint and yellow paint.$$),
    ('5e6546b9-dea5-4d32-80dd-ce5e29fb0b35', 2, $$The painters were busy. One painter was on a ladder. Another was hanging from the roof on a swing. “Can we help? ” asked Veena and Vinay.$$),
    ('5e6546b9-dea5-4d32-80dd-ce5e29fb0b35', 3, $$The painter gave each of them a brush. “Paint the inside of the gate,” he said to Veena. “Paint the outside of the gate,” he said to Vinay.$$),
    ('5e6546b9-dea5-4d32-80dd-ce5e29fb0b35', 4, $$They picked up two tins of paint and set to work. Veena painted one side of the gate. Vinay painted the other side of the gate.$$),
    ('5e6546b9-dea5-4d32-80dd-ce5e29fb0b35', 5, $$The paint fell on the ground. The paint fell on the wall. The paint fell on them.$$),
    ('5e6546b9-dea5-4d32-80dd-ce5e29fb0b35', 6, $$At last they finished. They wiped off the paint that had splashed on the ground. They wiped off the paint that had splashed on the wall.$$),
    ('5e6546b9-dea5-4d32-80dd-ce5e29fb0b35', 7, $$They wiped off the paint that had splashed on them.$$),
    ('5e6546b9-dea5-4d32-80dd-ce5e29fb0b35', 8, $$“I love my red gate! ” said Veena.$$),
    ('5e6546b9-dea5-4d32-80dd-ce5e29fb0b35', 9, $$“I love my green gate! ” said Vinay.$$),
    ('5e6546b9-dea5-4d32-80dd-ce5e29fb0b35', 10, $$“Oh, you have made a two-coloured gate! ” cried the painter. “Let us keep it that way! ” said Mother.$$),
    ('6733ac6c-5e59-4a15-801f-7cb0c54b6dd0', 0, $$A woman, carrying her baby, went into the forest to pick fruit.$$),
    ('6733ac6c-5e59-4a15-801f-7cb0c54b6dd0', 1, $$In the forest she found a tree with ripe fruit.$$),
    ('6733ac6c-5e59-4a15-801f-7cb0c54b6dd0', 2, $$She put down her sleeping baby and climbed the tree.$$),
    ('6733ac6c-5e59-4a15-801f-7cb0c54b6dd0', 3, $$An erotot from another community came by and saw the baby. Surprised, he asked himself, “Where is the mother of the baby? ”$$),
    ('6733ac6c-5e59-4a15-801f-7cb0c54b6dd0', 4, $$As he bent down, the sound of the chains on his neck woke the baby.$$),
    ('6733ac6c-5e59-4a15-801f-7cb0c54b6dd0', 5, $$He let the baby play with his chains. The baby laughed as he played.$$),
    ('6733ac6c-5e59-4a15-801f-7cb0c54b6dd0', 6, $$The woman looked down to see why the baby was laughing. She saw a strange man close to her baby.$$),
    ('6733ac6c-5e59-4a15-801f-7cb0c54b6dd0', 7, $$She was so afraid that she dropped her bag full of fruit.$$),
    ('6733ac6c-5e59-4a15-801f-7cb0c54b6dd0', 8, $$The erotot looked up and said, "Don't be afraid. I'm only playing with your beautiful baby. "$$),
    ('6733ac6c-5e59-4a15-801f-7cb0c54b6dd0', 9, $$So the woman came down from the tree.$$),
    ('6733ac6c-5e59-4a15-801f-7cb0c54b6dd0', 10, $$The erotot took off one of his chains. He gave it to the baby, and said, "Here is a gift for you. "$$),
    ('6733ac6c-5e59-4a15-801f-7cb0c54b6dd0', 11, $$Then he said to the woman, "Take your baby, take your bag, and go home. Tell your husband to move to a more peaceful village. Your baby has given me peace. "$$),
    ('68fbe614-d19c-4d76-a6f4-b0b9ccbf0e7d', 0, $$One day a caterpillar was very hungry. He looked for food to eat.$$),
    ('68fbe614-d19c-4d76-a6f4-b0b9ccbf0e7d', 1, $$He ate one banana, but he was still hungry.$$),
    ('68fbe614-d19c-4d76-a6f4-b0b9ccbf0e7d', 2, $$He ate two mangoes, but he was still hungry.$$),
    ('68fbe614-d19c-4d76-a6f4-b0b9ccbf0e7d', 3, $$He ate three papayas, but he was still hungry.$$),
    ('68fbe614-d19c-4d76-a6f4-b0b9ccbf0e7d', 4, $$He ate four pineapples, but he was still hungry.$$),
    ('68fbe614-d19c-4d76-a6f4-b0b9ccbf0e7d', 5, $$He ate five oranges, but he was still hungry.$$),
    ('68fbe614-d19c-4d76-a6f4-b0b9ccbf0e7d', 6, $$He ate six jambu, but he was still hungry.$$),
    ('68fbe614-d19c-4d76-a6f4-b0b9ccbf0e7d', 7, $$He was very big now. He made for himself a place to sleep.$$),
    ('68fbe614-d19c-4d76-a6f4-b0b9ccbf0e7d', 8, $$When he woke up, he was a beautiful butterfly!$$),
    ('6b5825ee-0afa-4bb5-9394-9e69120c3ca5', 0, $$What is it?$$),
    ('6b5825ee-0afa-4bb5-9394-9e69120c3ca5', 1, $$What is it? It hasn't got a trunk. It's not like me.$$),
    ('6b5825ee-0afa-4bb5-9394-9e69120c3ca5', 2, $$What is it? It hasn't got a tail. It's not like me.$$),
    ('6b5825ee-0afa-4bb5-9394-9e69120c3ca5', 3, $$What is it? Ugh! Where are its feathers?$$),
    ('6b5825ee-0afa-4bb5-9394-9e69120c3ca5', 4, $$What is it? Look at those tiny feet. It's not like us.$$),
    ('6b5825ee-0afa-4bb5-9394-9e69120c3ca5', 5, $$Do you think it's dangerous?$$),
    ('6b5825ee-0afa-4bb5-9394-9e69120c3ca5', 6, $$Do you think it wants to eat us? EDITED BY WADE$$),
    ('6b5825ee-0afa-4bb5-9394-9e69120c3ca5', 7, $$Achoo! Achoo!$$),
    ('6b5825ee-0afa-4bb5-9394-9e69120c3ca5', 8, $$Argh! Eek! Run!$$),
    ('6b5825ee-0afa-4bb5-9394-9e69120c3ca5', 9, $$It's chasing us!$$),
    ('6b5825ee-0afa-4bb5-9394-9e69120c3ca5', 10, $$Be careful. Come back.$$),
    ('6b5825ee-0afa-4bb5-9394-9e69120c3ca5', 11, $$What is it? It's a baby! Just like me!$$),
    ('6c0fbc11-808d-4c80-93b0-6dea501c0809', 0, $$Not here, not there. Where have you gone?$$),
    ('6c0fbc11-808d-4c80-93b0-6dea501c0809', 1, $$Not on the sofa. Not under the cot.$$),
    ('6c0fbc11-808d-4c80-93b0-6dea501c0809', 2, $$Not in the box. Not under my sister's frock.$$),
    ('6c0fbc11-808d-4c80-93b0-6dea501c0809', 3, $$Not under the pillow. Not in my bag. Sob, sob, where have you gone?$$),
    ('6c0fbc11-808d-4c80-93b0-6dea501c0809', 4, $$I have looked in every room, l have looked under every book.$$),
    ('6c0fbc11-808d-4c80-93b0-6dea501c0809', 5, $$I have looked under the chair, I have looked under the stool. Where have you gone?$$),
    ('6c0fbc11-808d-4c80-93b0-6dea501c0809', 6, $$Soon granny came back from her walk. "Look what I found in the park. "$$),
    ('6c0fbc11-808d-4c80-93b0-6dea501c0809', 7, $$"It can sway, it can bounce. It can spin, it can dangle. Ha-ha, hee-hee," said Granny with a giggle.$$),
    ('6c0fbc11-808d-4c80-93b0-6dea501c0809', 8, $$Oh Granny! Thank you so much! You have found my dear yo-yo!$$),
    ('6c0fbc11-808d-4c80-93b0-6dea501c0809', 9, $$"Yo-yo? What a funny name! What a funny toy! I want to play with it, It gives me so much joy! "$$),
    ('6c0fbc11-808d-4c80-93b0-6dea501c0809', 10, $$Giggle, giggle, giggling away, Granny played, with my little toy. For the rest of the day!$$),
    ('6c2a2c2f-e0d9-4ce8-85c9-2962ddb2584d', 0, $$Then Jesus told them a parable to show them they should always pray and not lose heart. He said:$$),
    ('6c2a2c2f-e0d9-4ce8-85c9-2962ddb2584d', 1, $$There was also a widow in that city who kept coming to him and saying, “Give me justice against my adversary. ”$$),
    ('6c2a2c2f-e0d9-4ce8-85c9-2962ddb2584d', 2, $$For a while he refused.$$),
    ('6c2a2c2f-e0d9-4ce8-85c9-2962ddb2584d', 3, $$But later on he said to himself, “Though I neither fear God nor have regard for people, yet because this widow keeps on bothering me, I will give her justice, or in the end she will wear me out by her unending pleas. ”$$),
    ('6c2a2c2f-e0d9-4ce8-85c9-2962ddb2584d', 4, $$$$),
    ('6c2a2c2f-e0d9-4ce8-85c9-2962ddb2584d', 5, $$And the Lord said, “Listen to what the unrighteous judge says! Won’t God give justice to his chosen ones, who cry out to him day and night? Will he delay long to help them? ”$$),
    ('6c2a2c2f-e0d9-4ce8-85c9-2962ddb2584d', 6, $$“I tell you, he will give them justice speedily. Nevertheless, when the Son of Man comes, will he find faith on earth? ”$$),
    ('6c784ea2-cfa2-4246-b1a3-c78401dc3a37', 0, $$This is Bekku. And that is me in the mirror.$$),
    ('6c784ea2-cfa2-4246-b1a3-c78401dc3a37', 1, $$This is what I love to do ... and this is what Bekku likes to do.$$),
    ('6c784ea2-cfa2-4246-b1a3-c78401dc3a37', 2, $$This is Bekku's favorite place, and that is mine. When Bekku sees a mouse she runs after it.$$),
    ('6c784ea2-cfa2-4246-b1a3-c78401dc3a37', 3, $$But if I see a mouse, I run from it.$$),
    ('6c784ea2-cfa2-4246-b1a3-c78401dc3a37', 4, $$Then when I run after my beeping car, Bekku scoots out through the door ajar.$$),
    ('6c784ea2-cfa2-4246-b1a3-c78401dc3a37', 5, $$When mamma gives us milk, we both go SLURP, SLURP. Then follow our loud BURP, BURPS!$$),
    ('6c784ea2-cfa2-4246-b1a3-c78401dc3a37', 6, $$We like different things - that is very plain. Our common love for milk, this will always remain!$$),
    ('6f2c6423-8dbe-4a27-a41a-ac1aae4ebd98', 0, $$This is Azizi. Azizi is my doll.$$),
    ('6f2c6423-8dbe-4a27-a41a-ac1aae4ebd98', 1, $$I like Azizi because he always smiles.$$),
    ('6f2c6423-8dbe-4a27-a41a-ac1aae4ebd98', 2, $$After I wake up I wash my face. Then I look for Azizi.$$),
    ('6f2c6423-8dbe-4a27-a41a-ac1aae4ebd98', 3, $$When I find Azizi I brush his hair.$$),
    ('6f2c6423-8dbe-4a27-a41a-ac1aae4ebd98', 4, $$When I eat breakfast I feed Azizi.$$),
    ('6f2c6423-8dbe-4a27-a41a-ac1aae4ebd98', 5, $$When I eat sweets I give one to Azizi.$$),
    ('6f2c6423-8dbe-4a27-a41a-ac1aae4ebd98', 6, $$But Azizi never eats his sweet. I wonder why!$$),
    ('6f2c6423-8dbe-4a27-a41a-ac1aae4ebd98', 7, $$I walk around the compound picking flowers.$$),
    ('6f2c6423-8dbe-4a27-a41a-ac1aae4ebd98', 8, $$I give a flower to Azizi. But he never says, “Thank you. ”$$),
    ('6f2c6423-8dbe-4a27-a41a-ac1aae4ebd98', 9, $$I wash Azizi clean before my mother bathes me.$$),
    ('6f2c6423-8dbe-4a27-a41a-ac1aae4ebd98', 10, $$I dress Azizi in red because I love the colour red.$$),
    ('6f2c6423-8dbe-4a27-a41a-ac1aae4ebd98', 11, $$When I go to sleep, I lay Azizi beside me.$$),
    ('6f7c4247-7d8d-4e91-b0fb-24c822607e43', 0, $$With my nose...$$),
    ('6f7c4247-7d8d-4e91-b0fb-24c822607e43', 1, $$... I smell dirty socks.$$),
    ('6f7c4247-7d8d-4e91-b0fb-24c822607e43', 2, $$... I smell beautiful flowers.$$),
    ('6f7c4247-7d8d-4e91-b0fb-24c822607e43', 3, $$With my eyes...$$),
    ('6f7c4247-7d8d-4e91-b0fb-24c822607e43', 4, $$... I see a balloon blowing away in the wind.$$),
    ('6f7c4247-7d8d-4e91-b0fb-24c822607e43', 5, $$... I see a happy cat.$$),
    ('6f7c4247-7d8d-4e91-b0fb-24c822607e43', 6, $$With my mouth...$$),
    ('6f7c4247-7d8d-4e91-b0fb-24c822607e43', 7, $$... I taste the salty sea.$$),
    ('6f7c4247-7d8d-4e91-b0fb-24c822607e43', 8, $$... I taste a juicy sweet orange.$$),
    ('6f7c4247-7d8d-4e91-b0fb-24c822607e43', 9, $$With my hand...$$),
    ('6f7c4247-7d8d-4e91-b0fb-24c822607e43', 10, $$... I take your hand.$$),
    ('7332e9c1-d60b-4ffe-a3bf-f0542a47f887', 0, $$Mummy has a new baby. It is a baby girl.$$),
    ('7332e9c1-d60b-4ffe-a3bf-f0542a47f887', 1, $$Her name is Sadie.$$),
    ('7332e9c1-d60b-4ffe-a3bf-f0542a47f887', 2, $$Sadie is very beautiful.$$),
    ('7332e9c1-d60b-4ffe-a3bf-f0542a47f887', 3, $$She was born in the month of June just like her mother.$$),
    ('7332e9c1-d60b-4ffe-a3bf-f0542a47f887', 4, $$She has big brown eyes.$$),
    ('7332e9c1-d60b-4ffe-a3bf-f0542a47f887', 5, $$I love my baby sister very much.$$),
    ('7332e9c1-d60b-4ffe-a3bf-f0542a47f887', 6, $$I run home from school everyday so I can play with her.$$),
    ('7665adb0-6335-4457-adf1-a7a72f006375', 0, $$Our Father in heaven,$$),
    ('7665adb0-6335-4457-adf1-a7a72f006375', 1, $$may your name be honoured.$$),
    ('7665adb0-6335-4457-adf1-a7a72f006375', 2, $$May your kingdom come.$$),
    ('7665adb0-6335-4457-adf1-a7a72f006375', 3, $$May your will be done on earth as it is in heaven.$$),
    ('7665adb0-6335-4457-adf1-a7a72f006375', 4, $$Give us today our daily bread.$$),
    ('7665adb0-6335-4457-adf1-a7a72f006375', 5, $$And forgive us our debts, as we ourselves have forgiven our debtors.$$),
    ('7665adb0-6335-4457-adf1-a7a72f006375', 6, $$$$),
    ('7665adb0-6335-4457-adf1-a7a72f006375', 7, $$And do not lead us into temptation,$$),
    ('7665adb0-6335-4457-adf1-a7a72f006375', 8, $$but deliver us from the evil one.$$),
    ('7665adb0-6335-4457-adf1-a7a72f006375', 9, $$For yours is the kingdom and the power and the glory forever. Amen.$$),
    ('79a4b0d1-2040-40c4-a955-980eaeb6e2cd', 0, $$Fireflies are small winged insects that glow in the dark. Why do they shine? What creates the spark within them? They’re bright and twinkling, like little stars. I wish I could glow like them, but I can’t. Can anyone tell me why they glow?$$),
    ('79a4b0d1-2040-40c4-a955-980eaeb6e2cd', 1, $$Imagine a dark moonless night, and you are in the woods with your classmates. You lose your way. What would you do? Would you try contacting your friends by flashing your torchlight?$$),
    ('79a4b0d1-2040-40c4-a955-980eaeb6e2cd', 2, $$Well, fireflies do the same. However, they have an unlimited supply of light within themselves! Fireflies never need to worry about fused light bulbs or electricity tariffs. They seem happy just to fly around and glow. Their glow is a signal to say, “Hey, look! I’m here! ”$$),
    ('79a4b0d1-2040-40c4-a955-980eaeb6e2cd', 3, $$The glow inside the firefly is produced by three things, a protein called luciferase , a pigment called luciferin , and oxygen . Protein are special molecules used to create body structures, such as muscles, bones and skin. Pigments are natural colouring substances found in animals and plants. When luciferase and luciferin meet inside the tiny belly of the firefly, they react with the oxygen already found in there.$$),
    ('79a4b0d1-2040-40c4-a955-980eaeb6e2cd', 4, $$Then, a celebration takes place like a soft firework display, and bright light is produced. This is the ‘glow’ of the firefly. Fireflies are bioluminescent, but they are not the only creatures that create light. Different types of fish and marine creatures also produce their own lights.$$),
    ('79a4b0d1-2040-40c4-a955-980eaeb6e2cd', 5, $$The glow of the firefly functions like a light switch. The firefly periodically turns its glow on and off. It sends a special ‘message’ from its brain to the ‘light organ’ inside its abdomen. Soon the chemical reaction begins and the glow is produced.$$),
    ('79a4b0d1-2040-40c4-a955-980eaeb6e2cd', 6, $$The male fireflies use their ‘glow’ to call out to the females. Once the females see this special glow, they respond by switching on their own lights. The fireflymates soon meet, and baby fireflies get created. Female fireflies prefer ‘flashy males’ that can blink the longest or at a faster pace.$$),
    ('79a4b0d1-2040-40c4-a955-980eaeb6e2cd', 7, $$The younger fireflies, or the larvae, mainly use their glow to chase predators away. The chemicals within their bodies are toxic, and have a horrible taste. Creatures that try to eat them, will spit them out, and go hunting elsewhere for tastier munchies.$$),
    ('79a4b0d1-2040-40c4-a955-980eaeb6e2cd', 8, $$There are more than 2,000 species of fireflies on this earth. During springtime, on dark nights, you may spot a few of them flitting around brightly. Though fireflies are tiny, when they group together, their glow can light up an entire garden. Sounds incredible, doesn’t it?$$),
    ('79a4b0d1-2040-40c4-a955-980eaeb6e2cd', 9, $$Amazing Facts$$),
    ('79a4b0d1-2040-40c4-a955-980eaeb6e2cd', 10, $$Amazing Facts$$),
    ('79a4b0d1-2040-40c4-a955-980eaeb6e2cd', 11, $$Do It Yourself$$),
    ('79a4b0d1-2040-40c4-a955-980eaeb6e2cd', 12, $$Do It Yourself$$),
    ('7ccef56e-0191-4b4b-8fd8-08f4ae184bca', 0, $$It was the Annual Haircut Day for Sringeri Srinivas.$$),
    ('7ccef56e-0191-4b4b-8fd8-08f4ae184bca', 1, $$Sringeri Srinivas left home as usual to go to the local barber.$$),
    ('7ccef56e-0191-4b4b-8fd8-08f4ae184bca', 2, $$But the barber said, “Today, I have no time to cut such long hair! ”$$),
    ('7ccef56e-0191-4b4b-8fd8-08f4ae184bca', 3, $$Feeling sad, Sringeri Srinivas went back home to ask his wife for help.$$),
    ('7ccef56e-0191-4b4b-8fd8-08f4ae184bca', 4, $$But his wife said, “Today, I have no time to cut such long hair! ”$$),
    ('7ccef56e-0191-4b4b-8fd8-08f4ae184bca', 5, $$Feeling a little angry, Sringeri Srinivas went to his friend, the tailor.$$),
    ('7ccef56e-0191-4b4b-8fd8-08f4ae184bca', 6, $$But the tailor said, “Today, I have no time to cut such long hair! ”$$),
    ('7ccef56e-0191-4b4b-8fd8-08f4ae184bca', 7, $$Now a little worried, Sringeri Srinivas went to one more friend, the carpenter.$$),
    ('7ccef56e-0191-4b4b-8fd8-08f4ae184bca', 8, $$But the carpenter said, “Today, I have no time to cut such long hair! ”$$),
    ('7ccef56e-0191-4b4b-8fd8-08f4ae184bca', 9, $$Poor Sringeri Srinivas. It seemed no one would cut his hair on this Annual Haircut Day.$$),
    ('7ccef56e-0191-4b4b-8fd8-08f4ae184bca', 10, $$In tears, he walked off by himself past the village forest.$$),
    ('7ccef56e-0191-4b4b-8fd8-08f4ae184bca', 11, $$He sat near a cave and cried loudly.$$),
    ('7ccef56e-0191-4b4b-8fd8-08f4ae184bca', 12, $$“The day is nearly over. How can I keep my promise to cut my hair? Oh God, help me! ”$$),
    ('7ccef56e-0191-4b4b-8fd8-08f4ae184bca', 13, $$The tiger sleeping peacefully inside the cave was very disturbed by all the noise.$$),
    ('7ccef56e-0191-4b4b-8fd8-08f4ae184bca', 14, $$He came out, roaring, waving his giant paws at Sringeri Srinivas.$$),
    ('7ccef56e-0191-4b4b-8fd8-08f4ae184bca', 15, $$Poor Sringeri Srinivas was so scared, so scared, so scared that ...$$),
    ('7ccef56e-0191-4b4b-8fd8-08f4ae184bca', 16, $$... all the hair fell off his head!$$),
    ('7ccef56e-0191-4b4b-8fd8-08f4ae184bca', 17, $$Sringeri Srinivas ran all the way back to the village. The tiger went back to sleep.$$),
    ('7ccef56e-0191-4b4b-8fd8-08f4ae184bca', 18, $$Now, Sringeri Srinivas will not need a haircut for a very long time.$$),
    ('7df1a879-2012-40df-bee2-ea837486411f', 0, $$Hello. My name is Kúùku. I am a girl .$$),
    ('7df1a879-2012-40df-bee2-ea837486411f', 1, $$This is my sister. Her name is Máá.$$),
    ('7df1a879-2012-40df-bee2-ea837486411f', 2, $$We live in a house. Our house is small.$$),
    ('7df1a879-2012-40df-bee2-ea837486411f', 3, $$The house has a door. The door is big.$$),
    ('7df1a879-2012-40df-bee2-ea837486411f', 4, $$The house has three windows. One double, two singles.$$),
    ('7df1a879-2012-40df-bee2-ea837486411f', 5, $$We have a cat. The cat is white.$$),
    ('7df1a879-2012-40df-bee2-ea837486411f', 6, $$The cat likes to run. It runs in the garden.$$),
    ('7df1a879-2012-40df-bee2-ea837486411f', 7, $$The garden has flowers. The flowers are red.$$),
    ('7df1a879-2012-40df-bee2-ea837486411f', 8, $$Máá plays with a cat. I read a book.$$),
    ('7df1a879-2012-40df-bee2-ea837486411f', 9, $$We are happy. We love our home$$),
    ('7e5a8e9d-28bd-4081-8509-fd081829eeff', 0, $$Dog is sleeping.$$),
    ('7e5a8e9d-28bd-4081-8509-fd081829eeff', 1, $$Dog wakes up.$$),
    ('7e5a8e9d-28bd-4081-8509-fd081829eeff', 2, $$Dog is eating breakfast.$$),
    ('7e5a8e9d-28bd-4081-8509-fd081829eeff', 3, $$Mary takes dog for a walk.$$),
    ('7e5a8e9d-28bd-4081-8509-fd081829eeff', 4, $$Dog is taking a nap.$$),
    ('7e5a8e9d-28bd-4081-8509-fd081829eeff', 5, $$Dog is eating lunch.$$),
    ('7e5a8e9d-28bd-4081-8509-fd081829eeff', 6, $$Dog is playing with his ball.$$),
    ('7e5a8e9d-28bd-4081-8509-fd081829eeff', 7, $$Dog is taking a bath in the tub.$$),
    ('7e5a8e9d-28bd-4081-8509-fd081829eeff', 8, $$Dog is playing his guitar and dancing.$$),
    ('7e5a8e9d-28bd-4081-8509-fd081829eeff', 9, $$Dog is having dinner.$$),
    ('7e5a8e9d-28bd-4081-8509-fd081829eeff', 10, $$Dog is in bed. Good night.$$),
    ('7edab369-1311-40fa-acba-3c3d7c23a9ce', 0, $$A cloud rolled along merrily in the sky.$$),
    ('7edab369-1311-40fa-acba-3c3d7c23a9ce', 1, $$The peacock said, “Why don’t you rain? I will dance for you. ”$$),
    ('7edab369-1311-40fa-acba-3c3d7c23a9ce', 2, $$The fish said, "Please rain. I need more water. "$$),
    ('7edab369-1311-40fa-acba-3c3d7c23a9ce', 3, $$The farmer said, “Please rain. I’ll plant seeds for the next crop. ”$$),
    ('7edab369-1311-40fa-acba-3c3d7c23a9ce', 4, $$Raju said, “If you rain, I’ll sail paper boats. ”$$),
    ('7edab369-1311-40fa-acba-3c3d7c23a9ce', 5, $$The cloud rained in a shower of shimmering drops.$$),
    ('7edab369-1311-40fa-acba-3c3d7c23a9ce', 6, $$The peacock spread its pretty feathers and danced.$$),
    ('7edab369-1311-40fa-acba-3c3d7c23a9ce', 7, $$The pond filled up. The fish was happy.$$),
    ('7edab369-1311-40fa-acba-3c3d7c23a9ce', 8, $$The farmer started planting seeds.$$),
    ('7edab369-1311-40fa-acba-3c3d7c23a9ce', 9, $$Splish! Splash! Splosh! Raju and his friends had a wonderful time in the puddles.$$),
    ('7edab369-1311-40fa-acba-3c3d7c23a9ce', 10, $$The cloud filled everybody's heart with joy. It moved on. All the children waved goodbye.$$),
    ('7edab369-1311-40fa-acba-3c3d7c23a9ce', 11, $$$$),
    ('7f92380a-2613-421a-a49f-d086f1a516a1', 0, $$Look at us. Do you want to be our friend?$$),
    ('7f92380a-2613-421a-a49f-d086f1a516a1', 1, $$My legs are very strong. I can run really fast with them.$$),
    ('7f92380a-2613-421a-a49f-d086f1a516a1', 2, $$And my arms... such a nice swing!$$),
    ('7f92380a-2613-421a-a49f-d086f1a516a1', 3, $$I like to draw. I use my hands for drawing.$$),
    ('7f92380a-2613-421a-a49f-d086f1a516a1', 4, $$Should I draw your picture? I can see you with my eyes.$$),
    ('7f92380a-2613-421a-a49f-d086f1a516a1', 5, $$The bird sings a sweet song. I can hear it with my ears.$$),
    ('7f92380a-2613-421a-a49f-d086f1a516a1', 6, $$I think Ma is making halwa. I can smell it with my nose.$$),
    ('7f92380a-2613-421a-a49f-d086f1a516a1', 7, $$Oh! This sugarcane is so tough! But my teeth are strong too!$$),
    ('7f92380a-2613-421a-a49f-d086f1a516a1', 8, $$It is very sweet. My tongue just told me.$$),
    ('7f92380a-2613-421a-a49f-d086f1a516a1', 9, $$I can sing. Should I sing you a song?$$),
    ('7f92380a-2613-421a-a49f-d086f1a516a1', 10, $$Ma says I have a good voice. Does it come from my throat?$$),
    ('80ff107f-ae67-4cac-8d57-e5bde2d17633', 0, $$Mat is a cat.$$),
    ('80ff107f-ae67-4cac-8d57-e5bde2d17633', 1, $$Mat sat on a hat.$$),
    ('80ff107f-ae67-4cac-8d57-e5bde2d17633', 2, $$Jig is a pig.$$),
    ('80ff107f-ae67-4cac-8d57-e5bde2d17633', 3, $$Jig sat on a wig.$$),
    ('80ff107f-ae67-4cac-8d57-e5bde2d17633', 4, $$Len is a hen. Len did not sit on a hat or a wig.$$),
    ('80ff107f-ae67-4cac-8d57-e5bde2d17633', 5, $$Len sat on ten eggs!$$),
    ('81d45baf-49bd-4321-9182-c7473e975d95', 0, $$Spider, spider, on the web.$$),
    ('81d45baf-49bd-4321-9182-c7473e975d95', 1, $$"Bee, Bee, come to me. "$$),
    ('81d45baf-49bd-4321-9182-c7473e975d95', 2, $$"No, no, Spider. Not me! "$$),
    ('81d45baf-49bd-4321-9182-c7473e975d95', 3, $$"Moth, Moth, come to me. "$$),
    ('81d45baf-49bd-4321-9182-c7473e975d95', 4, $$"No, no, Spider. Not me! "$$),
    ('81d45baf-49bd-4321-9182-c7473e975d95', 5, $$"Ant, Ant, come to me. "$$),
    ('81d45baf-49bd-4321-9182-c7473e975d95', 6, $$"No, no, Spider. Not me! "$$),
    ('81d45baf-49bd-4321-9182-c7473e975d95', 7, $$"Caterpillar, Caterpillar, come to me. "$$),
    ('81d45baf-49bd-4321-9182-c7473e975d95', 8, $$"No, no, Spider. Not me! "$$),
    ('81d45baf-49bd-4321-9182-c7473e975d95', 9, $$"Mosquito, Mosquito, come to me. "$$),
    ('81d45baf-49bd-4321-9182-c7473e975d95', 10, $$"No, no, Spider. Not me! "$$),
    ('81d45baf-49bd-4321-9182-c7473e975d95', 11, $$"Grasshopper, Grasshopper, come to me. "$$),
    ('81d45baf-49bd-4321-9182-c7473e975d95', 12, $$"No, no, Spider. Not me! "$$),
    ('81d45baf-49bd-4321-9182-c7473e975d95', 13, $$"Spider, Spider! Come to me. "$$),
    ('81d45baf-49bd-4321-9182-c7473e975d95', 14, $$"No, no, Bird. Not me! "$$),
    ('8556513d-be23-4945-bf27-cb4317497219', 0, $$I am Bintu. This is my friend, Bingo, the puppy.$$),
    ('8556513d-be23-4945-bf27-cb4317497219', 1, $$I like to tease Bingo. I tell him that I am better than he.$$),
    ('8556513d-be23-4945-bf27-cb4317497219', 2, $$He does not like it.$$),
    ('8556513d-be23-4945-bf27-cb4317497219', 3, $$“Look! I have a nose! ” I say.$$),
    ('8556513d-be23-4945-bf27-cb4317497219', 4, $$“Woof! ” says Bingo. That means he has a nose too.$$),
    ('8556513d-be23-4945-bf27-cb4317497219', 5, $$“Look! I have ears! ” I say.$$),
    ('8556513d-be23-4945-bf27-cb4317497219', 6, $$“Woof! ” says Bingo. That means he has ears too.$$),
    ('8556513d-be23-4945-bf27-cb4317497219', 7, $$“Look! I have eyes! ” I say.$$),
    ('8556513d-be23-4945-bf27-cb4317497219', 8, $$“Woof! ” says Bingo. That means he has eyes too.$$),
    ('8556513d-be23-4945-bf27-cb4317497219', 9, $$“Look! I have a tongue! ” I say.$$),
    ('8556513d-be23-4945-bf27-cb4317497219', 10, $$“Woof! ” says Bingo. That means he has a tongue too.$$),
    ('8556513d-be23-4945-bf27-cb4317497219', 11, $$“Look! I have can dance on my legs! ” I say.$$),
    ('8556513d-be23-4945-bf27-cb4317497219', 12, $$“Woof, woof, woof, woof, woof! ” says Bingo. That means he has legs too.$$),
    ('8556513d-be23-4945-bf27-cb4317497219', 13, $$“Look! I can think! ” I say.$$),
    ('8556513d-be23-4945-bf27-cb4317497219', 14, $$“Wooooooof! ” says Bingo. That means he can think too.$$),
    ('8556513d-be23-4945-bf27-cb4317497219', 15, $$“Look! I have hands! ” I say.$$),
    ('8556513d-be23-4945-bf27-cb4317497219', 16, $$“Grrr... ” says Bingo and turns around to show me his tail. That means he has a tail and I don’t.$$),
    ('8556513d-be23-4945-bf27-cb4317497219', 17, $$But I love Bingo, and he loves me!$$),
    ('8556513d-be23-4945-bf27-cb4317497219', 18, $$Can you name all these parts of your body?$$),
    ('86719656-00fb-416b-8482-793ccafe0364', 0, $$Why is the sky blue?$$),
    ('86719656-00fb-416b-8482-793ccafe0364', 1, $$It is not always blue. Is it?$$),
    ('86719656-00fb-416b-8482-793ccafe0364', 2, $$Why are leaves green?$$),
    ('86719656-00fb-416b-8482-793ccafe0364', 3, $$They are not always green. Are they?$$),
    ('86719656-00fb-416b-8482-793ccafe0364', 4, $$Why are bananas yellow?$$),
    ('86719656-00fb-416b-8482-793ccafe0364', 5, $$Ripe bananas are yellow. Raw bananas are green.$$),
    ('86719656-00fb-416b-8482-793ccafe0364', 6, $$Why are umbrellas black?$$),
    ('86719656-00fb-416b-8482-793ccafe0364', 7, $$All umbrellas are not black.$$),
    ('86719656-00fb-416b-8482-793ccafe0364', 8, $$Why is blood red?$$),
    ('86719656-00fb-416b-8482-793ccafe0364', 9, $$There is iron in the blood. That makes it red.$$),
    ('86719656-00fb-416b-8482-793ccafe0364', 10, $$Why is salt white? I don't know.$$),
    ('8bb25a45-52d8-44ef-9731-a6ed96be4ac4', 0, $$Suresh was a poor farmer.$$),
    ('8bb25a45-52d8-44ef-9731-a6ed96be4ac4', 1, $$Everyday he looked up to the sky for rain.$$),
    ('8bb25a45-52d8-44ef-9731-a6ed96be4ac4', 2, $$Everytime Clouds came and went away without giving rain.$$),
    ('8bb25a45-52d8-44ef-9731-a6ed96be4ac4', 3, $$There is outcry because of drought.$$),
    ('8bb25a45-52d8-44ef-9731-a6ed96be4ac4', 4, $$He prayed to God for rain.$$),
    ('8bb25a45-52d8-44ef-9731-a6ed96be4ac4', 5, $$He found the reason of drought.$$),
    ('8bb25a45-52d8-44ef-9731-a6ed96be4ac4', 6, $$He found permanent solution on drought. Plant and nourish trees and save nature.$$),
    ('8f0e7b55-73c4-41b0-9095-65d25ece1f2f', 0, $$This is a fat king.$$),
    ('8f0e7b55-73c4-41b0-9095-65d25ece1f2f', 1, $$The fat king has a thin dog. The fat king and his thin dog go for a walk.$$),
    ('8f0e7b55-73c4-41b0-9095-65d25ece1f2f', 2, $$The dog sees a bird. The dog runs after the bird.$$),
    ('8f0e7b55-73c4-41b0-9095-65d25ece1f2f', 3, $$The king runs after the dog.$$),
    ('8f0e7b55-73c4-41b0-9095-65d25ece1f2f', 4, $$They run and run. They run and run for many days.$$),
    ('8f0e7b55-73c4-41b0-9095-65d25ece1f2f', 5, $$The king catches the dog.$$),
    ('8f0e7b55-73c4-41b0-9095-65d25ece1f2f', 6, $$Now the fat king is thin.$$),
    ('9455894a-b5b1-475e-a06f-0ea256897a07', 0, $$Ball.$$),
    ('9455894a-b5b1-475e-a06f-0ea256897a07', 1, $$My ball.$$),
    ('9455894a-b5b1-475e-a06f-0ea256897a07', 2, $$My red ball.$$),
