    ('985f9b3a-bd32-4eaa-938a-a47c694c1ad7', 0, $$This is Naumu. She is my teacher.$$),
    ('985f9b3a-bd32-4eaa-938a-a47c694c1ad7', 1, $$Naumu uses crutches to walk.$$),
    ('985f9b3a-bd32-4eaa-938a-a47c694c1ad7', 2, $$This is Meta. He talks on the radio.$$),
    ('985f9b3a-bd32-4eaa-938a-a47c694c1ad7', 3, $$He is blind. He has white skin that sunburns easily.$$),
    ('985f9b3a-bd32-4eaa-938a-a47c694c1ad7', 4, $$This is Mari. Mari gardens.$$),
    ('985f9b3a-bd32-4eaa-938a-a47c694c1ad7', 5, $$Mari cannot hear. She speaks using her hands. This is called sign language.$$),
    ('985f9b3a-bd32-4eaa-938a-a47c694c1ad7', 6, $$This is Iauko. He is the best football player at my school.$$),
    ('985f9b3a-bd32-4eaa-938a-a47c694c1ad7', 7, $$Iauko has no hands. But he scores many goals for our team!$$),
    ('9c801b5e-a190-43e3-83a1-cabf69346bad', 0, $$My name is Natiang.$$),
    ('9c801b5e-a190-43e3-83a1-cabf69346bad', 1, $$I have four friends.$$),
    ('9c801b5e-a190-43e3-83a1-cabf69346bad', 2, $$Their names are Noakawir, Tou Mita, Kaupa and Talele.$$),
    ('9c801b5e-a190-43e3-83a1-cabf69346bad', 3, $$My friend Talele likes to play soccer.$$),
    ('9c801b5e-a190-43e3-83a1-cabf69346bad', 4, $$My friend Kaupa likes to swim.$$),
    ('9c801b5e-a190-43e3-83a1-cabf69346bad', 5, $$My friend Noakawir likes to play hide-and-seek.$$),
    ('9c801b5e-a190-43e3-83a1-cabf69346bad', 6, $$My friend Tou Mita likes to read.$$),
    ('9c801b5e-a190-43e3-83a1-cabf69346bad', 7, $$Me? I like to do all the things they like to do.$$),
    ('9c801b5e-a190-43e3-83a1-cabf69346bad', 8, $$I play soccer with Talele.$$),
    ('9c801b5e-a190-43e3-83a1-cabf69346bad', 9, $$I swim with Kaupa.$$),
    ('9c801b5e-a190-43e3-83a1-cabf69346bad', 10, $$I play hide-and-seek with Noakawir.$$),
    ('9c801b5e-a190-43e3-83a1-cabf69346bad', 11, $$Now what do you like to do?$$),
    ('9c801b5e-a190-43e3-83a1-cabf69346bad', 12, $$Come, play soccer with us.$$),
    ('9c801b5e-a190-43e3-83a1-cabf69346bad', 13, $$Come, swim with us.$$),
    ('9c801b5e-a190-43e3-83a1-cabf69346bad', 14, $$Come, play hide-and-seek with us.$$),
    ('9c801b5e-a190-43e3-83a1-cabf69346bad', 15, $$Come, read with us!$$),
    ('9dace09b-04f4-4a5a-9787-c25544ab4046', 0, $$Years ago, a group of horned animals decided to have a big party high up in the mountains. They only invited other animals with horns. No one else.$$),
    ('9dace09b-04f4-4a5a-9787-c25544ab4046', 1, $$When the pig heard about the party, he thought, “I don’t have any horns. What am I going to do? ”$$),
    ('9dace09b-04f4-4a5a-9787-c25544ab4046', 2, $$The next day, he had an idea. He’d stick some horns to his head with wax!$$),
    ('9dace09b-04f4-4a5a-9787-c25544ab4046', 3, $$It worked! The pig felt very clever when he was allowed into the party. The problem was that the party was taking place close to the sun.$$),
    ('9dace09b-04f4-4a5a-9787-c25544ab4046', 4, $$When the party started heating up, the wax began to melt and his horns started to fall off.$$),
    ('9dace09b-04f4-4a5a-9787-c25544ab4046', 5, $$The horned animals were shocked. “Who’s that one with no horns? Why did he come here? ” they asked.$$),
    ('9dace09b-04f4-4a5a-9787-c25544ab4046', 6, $$The king of the animals commanded, “Grab that pig and throw him down to earth! ” So all the animals did what the king commanded.$$),
    ('9dace09b-04f4-4a5a-9787-c25544ab4046', 7, $$They grabbed the pig and threw him down to earth.$$),
    ('9dace09b-04f4-4a5a-9787-c25544ab4046', 8, $$Poor pig! When he fell, he landed on his nose, and his nose was flattened into a snout.$$),
    ('9dace09b-04f4-4a5a-9787-c25544ab4046', 9, $$Their job done, all the other animals returned to the party. They ate and danced all night. And the king was happy.$$),
    ('9dace09b-04f4-4a5a-9787-c25544ab4046', 10, $$So don’t be surprised when you see the pig’s flat snout, because it’s been that way ever since.$$),
    ('9ebd7300-edfc-4359-a303-10aaf0ebc919', 0, $$Joy played all the day.$$),
    ('9ebd7300-edfc-4359-a303-10aaf0ebc919', 1, $$Her mother told her to wash.$$),
    ('9ebd7300-edfc-4359-a303-10aaf0ebc919', 2, $$She picked up her tooth brush.$$),
    ('9ebd7300-edfc-4359-a303-10aaf0ebc919', 3, $$Her mother put water in basin for her.$$),
    ('9ebd7300-edfc-4359-a303-10aaf0ebc919', 4, $$She dried her face.$$),
    ('9ebd7300-edfc-4359-a303-10aaf0ebc919', 5, $$She joined her sister to sleep.$$),
    ('9ebd7300-edfc-4359-a303-10aaf0ebc919', 6, $$In the morning she brushed her teeth.$$),
    ('9ebd7300-edfc-4359-a303-10aaf0ebc919', 7, $$Her mother helped her dress up.$$),
    ('9ebd7300-edfc-4359-a303-10aaf0ebc919', 8, $$She tied her shoes.$$),
    ('9ebd7300-edfc-4359-a303-10aaf0ebc919', 9, $$Joy goes to school.$$),
    ('9ebd7300-edfc-4359-a303-10aaf0ebc919', 10, $$Joy is in class.$$),
    ('9fdf0e7f-9ed0-49a7-95a3-5514e4a6b5f7', 0, $$Anu loves to look at things, big things and small. Houses on hills, ants on a wall.$$),
    ('9fdf0e7f-9ed0-49a7-95a3-5514e4a6b5f7', 1, $$Things in the kitchen, things on the shelf. Things in the garden, things on herself.$$),
    ('9fdf0e7f-9ed0-49a7-95a3-5514e4a6b5f7', 2, $$Anu sees patterns and shapes everywhere, nothing at all can escape her stare!$$),
    ('9fdf0e7f-9ed0-49a7-95a3-5514e4a6b5f7', 3, $$Spots on a ladybird, circles in trees, shapes made by people, shapes made by bees.$$),
    ('9fdf0e7f-9ed0-49a7-95a3-5514e4a6b5f7', 4, $$Lines on a leaf, just like lines on her hand. The marks of her feet in wet seaside sand.$$),
    ('9fdf0e7f-9ed0-49a7-95a3-5514e4a6b5f7', 5, $$Waves in the water, waves in her hair. Mushrooms on tree trunks, birds in the air.$$),
    ('9fdf0e7f-9ed0-49a7-95a3-5514e4a6b5f7', 6, $$Words in a book that can take her to places, full of new colours, new stories, new faces.$$),
    ('9fdf0e7f-9ed0-49a7-95a3-5514e4a6b5f7', 7, $$Things of the colour that she loves best - RED! The three wiggly hairs on her brother Boo's head.$$),
    ('9fdf0e7f-9ed0-49a7-95a3-5514e4a6b5f7', 8, $$Sprinkles on the cake Daddy baked today, like the stars that twinkle at her from far away.$$),
    ('9fdf0e7f-9ed0-49a7-95a3-5514e4a6b5f7', 9, $$Rabbits in clouds floating up in the sky. Elephants in shadows - come, give it a try!$$),
    ('9fdf0e7f-9ed0-49a7-95a3-5514e4a6b5f7', 10, $$Anu is happy with the things that she sees. Do you also see what little Anu sees?$$),
    ('a01270f6-69d6-4eba-b6da-253098fe015e', 0, $$It's not easy being a tiger. Yes, tigers are beautiful and fierce.$$),
    ('a01270f6-69d6-4eba-b6da-253098fe015e', 1, $$But tigers are also big and heavy. This makes it difficult for them to hunt for food.$$),
    ('a01270f6-69d6-4eba-b6da-253098fe015e', 2, $$Out of every twenty times a tiger hunts, it eats only once.$$),
    ('a01270f6-69d6-4eba-b6da-253098fe015e', 3, $$When a tiger moves through the forest, KHAU! KHAU! KHAK! The langur calls, just like an old man coughing! KHAU! KHAU! KHAK!$$),
    ('a01270f6-69d6-4eba-b6da-253098fe015e', 4, $$AWOOOO! HAWOOOO! The barking deer calls, like a scared dog! AWOOOO! HAWOOOO!$$),
    ('a01270f6-69d6-4eba-b6da-253098fe015e', 5, $$OOW! OOW! OOW! The spotted deer calls, like a little bird! OOW! OOW! OOW!$$),
    ('a01270f6-69d6-4eba-b6da-253098fe015e', 6, $$The whole forest knows the tiger is here! AHUUUN? AHUUUN? The tiger wonders, where has everyone gone?$$),
    ('a4b21445-88df-4315-9c6c-e6e4d7e7f196', 0, $$Why is sea water salty?$$),
    ('a4b21445-88df-4315-9c6c-e6e4d7e7f196', 1, $$It tastes salty because there is salt in the sea.$$),
    ('a4b21445-88df-4315-9c6c-e6e4d7e7f196', 2, $$Why is the chocolate sweet?$$),
    ('a4b21445-88df-4315-9c6c-e6e4d7e7f196', 3, $$It tastes sweet because there is sugar in it.$$),
    ('a4b21445-88df-4315-9c6c-e6e4d7e7f196', 4, $$Why is a lime sour?$$),
    ('a4b21445-88df-4315-9c6c-e6e4d7e7f196', 5, $$The acid in the lime makes it sour.$$),
    ('a4b21445-88df-4315-9c6c-e6e4d7e7f196', 6, $$Is there salt in tears?$$),
    ('a4b21445-88df-4315-9c6c-e6e4d7e7f196', 7, $$Yes, there is.$$),
    ('a4b21445-88df-4315-9c6c-e6e4d7e7f196', 8, $$Is there sugar in a mango?$$),
    ('a4b21445-88df-4315-9c6c-e6e4d7e7f196', 9, $$Yes, there is sugar in ripe mangoes.$$),
    ('a4b21445-88df-4315-9c6c-e6e4d7e7f196', 10, $$Is there acid in curds? Yes, there is some acid in curds.$$)
  ) AS v(source_id, page_index, text)
  JOIN books b
    ON b.source_platform = 'bloom' AND b.source_id = v.source_id
ON CONFLICT (book_id, page_index) DO NOTHING;

-- ───────── [적재검증] 트랜잭션 안 ─────────
